SEQUENCE:1
CREATED:20260914T143339Z
DESCRIPTION:<b><a href="https://www.eventbrite.com/e/2003021882370?aff=odd
 tdtcreator" target="_blank">Register here</a></b><p>Join volunteer and lan
 d steward Brian for a walking stick whittling workshop along the Eno! Lear
 n about stewardship and natural resource management while collecting sapli
 ngs to create a hand-carved walking stick to take home. Bring a pocketknif
 e\, a chair\, water and something to snack on while you learn the basics o
 f wood whittling with Brian on a peaceful Saturday morning at the Confluen
 ce Natural Area in Hillsborough.</p><p><strong>Suggested ages</strong> 12 
 and up. Limited to 25 participants. $15 for the general public\, $9 for En
 o River Association members and children under 18.</p><p><strong>Direction
 s</strong>: Meet at the pavilion beside the parking lot. The address is 42
 14 Highland Farm Rd\, Hillsborough\, NC 27278.</p><u></u><u></u><u></u><u>
 </u><u></u>
LAST-MODIFIED:20261014T140518Z
LOCATION:4214 Highland Farm Rd\, Hillsborough\, NC 27278\, USA
STATUS:CONFIRMED
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
X-SOURCE:Eno River Association
END:VEVENT
