X-SOURCE-ID:downtowndurham
X-SOURCE:Downtown Durham Inc
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20261114T160000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20261114T170000
DTSTAMP:20260609T170504Z
CREATED:20260609T170504Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260609T170504Z
UID:10232980-1794672000-1794675600@downtowndurham.com
SUMMARY:Downtown Durham African American Historian-Guided Tour
DESCRIPTION:Durham: the mecca of black capitalism and the center of North Carolina’s African American business community. Join a local historian on this guided walking tour of Durham’s Black Wall Street\, hearing the stories of how a humble sharecropper became the owner of the largest black-ned company in American history\, and seeing some of the sites related to their stories. Learn how businessmen\, labor organizers\, educated academics\, and craftsmen each contributed to the unique history of Durham’s African American community.
URL:https://downtowndurham.com/event/downtown-durham-african-american-historian-guided-tour/2026-11-14/
LOCATION:CCB Plaza\, 201 Corcoran St\, Durham\, 27703
CATEGORIES:History,Walk
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://downtowndurham.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/MFBank-1.jpg
ORGANIZER;CN="Triangle Walking Tours":MAILTO:andrew@nason.net
GEO:35.996654;-78.901784
