UID:event_317138203@meetup.com
SEQUENCE:1
DTSTAMP:20261114T061547Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20261114T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20261114T223000
SUMMARY:Ballroom Dance with Stardusters!
DESCRIPTION:Raleigh & Triangle Activities Meetup Group\nNo partner require
 d\, beautiful floor\, lesson included\, friendly dancers. Typical attendan
 ce is 1-2 MeetUp people and 45-60 general public. Plenty of people to meet
  and dance with!\n\nStardusters is a local non-profit that hosts ballroom 
 dances every second Saturday. Join us!\n\n### **-Masks are optional.**\n\n
 * **The CDC says the best way to minimize the chance of covid infection is
  to have circulating fresh air. We will open windows and run fans to get a
 s close to this ideal as we can.**\n* **Admission is $15\, cash or check.*
 *\n* **As always\, we provide a printed playlist of all songs together wit
 h the recommended dance.**\n* General dancing after the lesson will includ
 e all ballroom dances plus selections of Salsa\, Bachata\, Country 2 Step\
 , Night Club 2 Step and West Coast Swing\n* **Water and a small selection 
 of snacks will be provided.**\n* **No partner needed.**\n\n## **The Centur
 y Center 100 North Greensboro Street\, Carrboro\, NC**\n\n**Click here to 
 see a map of recommended parking areas: [Parking Areas](https://www.townof
 carrboro.org/DocumentCenter/View/6718/CC-Color-Parking-Map)**\n\n# **Free 
 Dance Lesson from 7:20-8:15**\n\n# **Ballroom Dancing from 8:15 - 10:40 PM
 **\n\n# **$15 admission**\n\n**Free Refreshments**\n\n## **[Visit and Like
  Us on Facebook](http://www.facebook.com/trianglestardusters.org) https://
 www.facebook.com/trianglestardusters.org**
URL;VALUE=URI:https://www.meetup.com/raleigh-triangle-activities/events/31
 7138203/
STATUS:CONFIRMED
CREATED:20261025T232229Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20261025T232229Z
CLASS:PUBLIC
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Duke Arts": "https://calendar.duke.edu/show?fq=id:CAL-8a002ad8-9f611855-019f-61c61d81-00001120demobedework@mysite.edu"}
X-SOURCE-ID:calendar_index_ics
X-SOURCE:Duke Arts, Duke University

CATEGORIES:Arts
CATEGORIES:Utilities
CATEGORIES:Concert/Music
CATEGORIES:Main
CONTACT;X-BEDEWORK-UID=00f1fcdb-0f068baf-010f-068baf83-00000004:None
CREATED:20260714T175641Z
DESCRIPTION:Explore three centuries of musical innovation as faculty violi
 nist Gabriel Richard presents "The Three Bs: Bach\, Bartók\, Boulez-Persp
 ectives on Form from the Baroque to the Contemporary."\n\nThe program tra
 ces the evolution of musical form through a violin transcription of Bach'
 s BWV 542\, Bartók's Sonata for Solo Violin\, Boulez's Anthèmes I\, and B
 ach's Partita No. 2 for Solo Violin. Moving from the intricate architectu
 re of the Baroque to the bold musical languages of the 20th century\, the
  recital reveals striking connections among three composers whose works c
 ontinually challenge and redefine the possibilities of sound.\n\nThis eve
 nt is free and open to the public. All are welcome.
DURATION:PT2H
DTSTAMP:20260901T150548Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20261114T200000
LAST-MODIFIED:20260901T150548Z
LOCATION;X-BEDEWORK-UID=18832edc-1b27e154-011b-281c3073-00000027:East Duke
  201 - Nelson Music Room
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Faculty Recital: Gabriel Richard — The Three Bs
