X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Nchumanities": "https://nchumanities.org/event/jewish-history-trolley-tours/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:nchumanities
X-SOURCE:NC Humanities Council
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20261115T130000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20261115T160000
DTSTAMP:20261109T183250Z
CREATED:20261109T183250Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20261109T183250Z
UID:10001467-1794747600-1794758400@nchumanities.org
SUMMARY:Jewish History Trolley Tours
DESCRIPTION:Take a journey to uncover Raleigh’s Jewish heritage and history\, starting with Raleigh’s first Jewish resident\, Moses Mordecai\, the namesake of Mordecai Historic Park. We’ll learn about Michael and Regina Grausman\, who hosted Raleigh’s first synagogue in their home. And new this year\, each row of the trolley holds a trip packet with photos and small maps to help us explore the buildings\, sites\, and lives of those who built Raleigh’s Jewish community. \nThese hour-long tours begin and end at Mordecai Historic Park at 1:00 pm\, 2:00 pm and 3:00 pm. Please arrive 15 minutes early to check tickets and to meet the trolley on time. Tickets can be purchased online at reclink.raleighnc.gov or in person at the Mordecai Visitor Center. For more information\, call 919-996-4364.
URL:https://nchumanities.org/event/jewish-history-trolley-tours/
LOCATION:Mordecai Historic Park\, 1 Mimosa Street\, Raleigh\, NC\, 27604\, United States
CATEGORIES:Humanities Sector Event
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://nchumanities.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/2025-RaleighTrolley-Mordecai044-scaled.jpg
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Triangleland": "https://triangleland.org/event/schenck-forest-umstead-loop"}
X-SOURCE-ID:triangleland
X-SOURCE:Triangle Land Conservancy
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20261115T130000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20261115T160000
DTSTAMP:20261026T202929Z
CREATED:20261005T022802Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20261026T202929Z
UID:10000121-1794747600-1794758400@triangleland.org
SUMMARY:Schenck Forest & Walton Farm Tour
DESCRIPTION:Join TLC on this special partner hike through Schenck Forest and Walton Farm! \nNaturalist and TLC Trail guide\, Julie Hall\, will guide you on this 5-mile hike through Schenck Forest and a short section of the City of Raleigh Greenway to reach the Walton Farm. Mary Walton is looking forward to speaking with the group about the Conservation Easement process and working with TLC on this partnership to protect her farm. We will get to walk through a portion of the farm\, and then head back on the greenway and through Schenk Forest to complete a loop.\n\nThis is a free event\, but preregistration is required. Schenck Forest serves as a working forest and outdoor laboratory for North Carolina State University students\, so there is a strict no dog policy. 
URL:https://triangleland.org/event/schenck-forest-umstead-loop
LOCATION:Carl Alwin Schenck Memorial Forest\, Reedy Creek Rd\, Raleigh\, NC\, 27607\, United States
ORGANIZER;CN="Amaya Horner":MAILTO:ahorner@triangleland.org
END:VEVENT
