UID:tag:localist.com\,2008:EventInstance_54152808493946
DTSTART:20261115T200000Z
DTEND:20261115T220000Z
DESCRIPTION:This event has been canceled due to weather concerns. \n\n \n\n
 *Registration required to reserve your spot* Follow the link above to rese
 rve your spot.        The registration link will be available starting 11/
 1/26.\n\nJoin a Lake James State Park Ranger for a boat tour on beautiful 
 Lake James! Participants will enjoy approximately two hours on the water w
 hile exploring key landmarks around the park\, and learning about its fasc
 inating history and natural resources. As we cruise along the shoreline\, 
 we will keep our eyes open for wildlife\, waterfowl\, and Bald Eagles. Thi
 s will be an opportunity to experience Lake James State Park from a differ
 ent perspective with a focus on the Paddy's Creek and Linville River areas
  of the lake.\n\nMeeting Location: Lake James State Park Paddy's Creek Acc
 ess- East Shelter\nDuration: Approximately 2 hours 3:00PM-5:00PM\n\nPlease
  Bring: Personal floatation device(we can provide basic PFDs if needed)\, 
 water\, sunglasses\, and a jacket \n\nThings to know: Participants may bri
 ng cameras or other items they feel will make them comfortable but please 
 pack light as space will be limited on the boat. Everybody must register p
 rior to the event to have a spot on the boat. Registration is only for the
  name listed\, children or spouses have to register separately. Space is l
 imited to 6 people. If you cannot make it please call us so we can open th
 e spot for another person.
GEO:35.760718;-81.882276
LOCATION:Lake James State Park - Paddy's Creek Access\, East Shelter
SUMMARY:An Evening on the Lake - CANCELED 
URL;VALUE=URI:https://events.dncr.nc.gov/event/an-evening-on-the-lake-2150
