DESCRIPTION:Seed Stories is a lecture series hosted by the UNC American Ind
 ian Center that explores Indigenous knowledge\, ethnobotany\, and agricult
 ural traditions. This upcoming Seed Stories Lecture will be held at the Am
 erican Indian Center on Tuesday\, Nov. 17 from 12:30-1:30 PM. For this lec
 ture\, we are inviting Darlene Graham\, a citizen of the Waccamaw-Siouan T
 ribe\, to speak about her experience working with her tribe's Healing Gree
 n Space! CLE credit will be provided.
