UID:tag:localist.com\,2008:EventInstance_53983028976821
DTSTART:20261118T170000Z
DTEND:20261118T180000Z
DESCRIPTION:Authors Bill and Chris Barber will discuss their newest book\, 
 Forgotten Patriots of the Albemarle. Their research includes more than 700
  profiles of Patriots from the Edenton Military District for whom document
 ation is available to confirm their participation in the American Revoluti
 on. Others served in the North Carolina Provincial Congress or in other po
 litical positions\, while a small number provided needed goods and service
 s for the cause. Most patriots in the book have been all but forgotten. In
  addition\, the authors explore the unique challenges faced by the people 
 of the Edenton Military District.
GEO:36.296532;-76.219757
LOCATION:Museum of the Albemarle\, Gaither Auditorium
SUMMARY:History for Lunch: Forgotten Patriots of the Albemarle
