UID:tag:localist.com\,2008:EventInstance_54312518351554
DTSTART:20261119T190000Z
DTEND:20261119T210000Z
DESCRIPTION:Ever wonder how experienced paddlers decide when and where to g
 o? Learn how to “read” the water by understanding tides\, currents\, w
 ind\, weather\, and other conditions that can make every paddle different.
  We’ll put these skills into practice by working together to plan a kaya
 k trip using local maps\, forecasts\, and tide information. Leave with the
  knowledge and confidence to start planning your own adventures on the wat
 er.  Meet in the auditorium of the visitor center.
GEO:34.670531;-77.143056
LOCATION:Hammocks Beach State Park
SUMMARY:Reading the Water
URL;VALUE=URI:https://events.dncr.nc.gov/event/reading-the-water
CATEGORIES:Education Programs
CATEGORIES:Outdoor & Recreation
END:VEVENT
