X-SOURCE-ID:triangleland
X-SOURCE:Triangle Land Conservancy
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20261120T093000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20261120T113000
DTSTAMP:20261014T195607Z
CREATED:20261014T190058Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20261014T195607Z
UID:10000125-1795167000-1795174200@triangleland.org
SUMMARY:Trail Talks with TLC: Williamson
DESCRIPTION:Join TLC staff for guided nature journaling at Williamson Nature Preserve!\nSlow down and connect with nature with Senior Volunteer and Outreach Associate\, Amaya Horner! Amaya will give a brief history of Williamson Nature Preserve and talk about the types of programs that this working farm and public preserve offers. Then\, we will navigate Two Ponds Loop\, making stops along the way to collect observations about the world around us using nature journaling methods curated by naturalist and educator\, John Muir Laws.\n\nPlease bring your own journal and writing utensils\, but we will have some extra materials on hand. Participants will receive a Quick Start Guide to Nature Journaling zine written by John Muir Laws and the Wild Wonder Foundation to take home! This will be a slow\, 1.5 mile hike on uneven terrain. Bring a full water bottle and a mat or blanket to sit on for the still moments on trail.  This event is free\, but preregistration is required.\n\n 
URL:https://triangleland.org/event/trail-talks-with-tlc-williamson
LOCATION:Williamson Farm and Nature Preserve\, 4429 Old Country Mial Rd\, Raleigh\, 27610\, United States
ORGANIZER;CN="Amaya Horner":MAILTO:ahorner@triangleland.org
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Triangleland": "https://triangleland.org/event/nature-storytime-forest-detectives-2"}
X-SOURCE-ID:triangleland
X-SOURCE:Triangle Land Conservancy
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20261120T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20261120T113000
DTSTAMP:20261027T210421Z
CREATED:20261027T210421Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20261027T210421Z
UID:10000130-1795168800-1795174200@triangleland.org
SUMMARY:Nature Storytime: Forest Detectives
DESCRIPTION:Become a Forest Detective at our monthly Nature Storytime!\nEngage your sense of smell\, sight\, sound\, and wonder! This month’s story time will invite everyone to learn about the cycles and secrets of nature through nature stories\, nature games\, and a short ramble through the Brumley Nature Preserve. Join a TLC educator for this monthly story series where you can meet other families in your community and learn about nature. This month's nature stories are: "All Around Us" By Xelena Gomez and "Beneath" by Cori Doerrfeld. This program is designed for kids age 3-7 and their grownups. Please register all members of the family attending\, including children and adults. This event is free\, but preregistration is required:
URL:https://triangleland.org/event/nature-storytime-forest-detectives-2
LOCATION:Brumley South Nature Preserve\, 3055 New Hope Church Rd\, Chapel Hill\, NC\, 27514\, United States
END:VEVENT
