BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-ID:gcal_newhopeaudubon
SUMMARY:NHBA Bird Outing
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20261125T080000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20261125T110000
DTSTAMP:20261114T061623Z
UID:3b2tmene29eg2tc51kuot210pp@google.com
RECURRENCE-ID;TZID=America/New_York:20261125T080000
SEQUENCE:0
CREATED:20261027T174048Z
DESCRIPTION:For questions\, contact Don Pelly at donpelly73@gmail.com for
  questions. The location will be Mason Farm Biological Preserve in Chapel
  Hill\, located behind the Finley Golf Course at 500 Finley Golf Course Rd
 .\, Chapel Hill. \n\nGoing south on US 15-501\, turn left onto Old Mason 
 Farm Rd. at the stop light. After about a mile\, turn right at the entranc
 e to Finley and drive around the back of the clubhouse to the parking lot.
  Drive through the parking lot and continue onto a paved road at the back\
 , right-hand corner of the lot. Follow this road about 100 feet (just past
  the practice putting green) until you come to a fork in the road and take
  the right-hand fork onto a gravel road. Go about 0.5 miles until you come
  to a junction. Turn right to cross a concrete low water crossing across M
 organ Creek. Go over the low water crossing and up the embankment to meet 
 in the parking lot. \n\nHeavy rains prior to the event may make the low w
 ater crossing impassible and result in a location change.\n\nThis outing i
 s sponsored by the New Hope Bird Alliance.\n\nOutings usually last 2-3 hou
 rs. No reservations or sign-up needed. If there is a large turnout for any
  particular outing\, we may split into two groups. We do recommend carpool
 ing for families or friend pods\; while we love pets\, there is a ‘no-pe
 t’ policy for bird outings. New birders and birders of all skill levels 
 are welcome. \n\nPlease wear long pants\, socks\, and sturdy shoes (ticks 
 and chiggers may be present). Sun and bug protection are also recommended.
  Bring snacks and water if you like. Heavy rain will result in cancellatio
 n.
LAST-MODIFIED:20261102T023928Z
STATUS:CONFIRMED
TRANSP:OPAQUE
X-SOURCE:New Hope Bird Alliance
END:VEVENT
