DESCRIPTION:Join the North Carolina State Capitol and Governor Josh Stein f
 or the annual tree-lighting tradition on Tuesday\, Dec. 1. \n\nThe lightin
 g of the State Christmas Tree at the Capitol is considered the official st
 art of the holiday season in the Tar Heel State. The festivities will begi
 n on Capitol Square at 5:30 p.m. with luminaries and holiday music perform
 ed by the Raleigh Concert Band. The governor and dignitaries will make the
 ir way to the South grounds just after 6 p.m. to officially begin the cere
 mony. The lit tree will be visible the length of Fayetteville Street. This
  year\, State Employees’ Credit Union will provide refreshments on the s
 outh plaza – and even Santa is scheduled to make an appearance! \n\nFoll
 owing the ceremony\, visitors are invited into the Capitol to experience t
 he holiday decorations and hear performances by local musicians. The Capit
 ol is open 6:30-7:30 p.m.\n\nThe State Christmas tree\, a real Fraser fir\
 , comes to the Capitol from the mountains of North Carolina. This year\, t
 he State Tree is sponsored by State Employees’ Credit Union.\n\nThe Capi
 tol will host a Holiday Open House and music in the rotunda from Thursday\
 , Dec. 3 – Saturday\, Dec. 5 (Thursday\, 10 a.m.-11 a.m\, 12 p.m.-2 p.m\
 , and 3 p.m.-4 p\,m\, Friday: 10 a.m.-12 p.m\, 1 p.m.-4 p.m.\; Saturday: 1
 0 a.m.- 12 p.m. 1 p.m. - 4 p.m.). Other sponsors of the holiday festivitie
 s include the State Capitol Foundation\, the N.C. Department of Natural an
 d Cultural Resources Division of State Historic Sites and the N.C. Departm
 ent of Administration-Facility Management.\n\nAll Capitol events are free\
 , and reservations are not needed or accepted. For additional information\
 , please call (984) 867-8340. The State Capitol is located at 1 East Edent
 on Street in downtown Raleigh.
GEO:35.780431;-78.639946
LOCATION:State Capitol
SUMMARY:State Tree Lighting & Holiday Open House
URL;VALUE=URI:https://events.dncr.nc.gov/event/state-tree-lighting-holiday-
 open-house-6207
CATEGORIES:Celebrations & Commemorations
END:VEVENT
