SUMMARY:Holiday Greenery: Build Your Own Wreath
DESCRIPTION:Duke Gardens’ Michelle Rawlins\, Ruth Mary Meyer Japanese Garden Horticulturist\, and Megan Brown\, horticulturist of the Gateway Gardens\, will demonstrate how to construct a holiday wreath for your front door using fresh-cut greenery from the Gardens. Each participant will learn how to build a wreath using provided greenery and other interesting botanical components.  Please bring a pair of hand pruners and any additional adornments you would like to include. All other materials will be provided. \nFee: $78; 20% discount for Duke Gardens members with discount code. \nParking: Parking fees apply. \nLocation: Onsite at Duke Gardens. \nAccessibility: This will be a small group program that takes place seated indoors in a location that requires traveling on a combination of paved and unpaved surfaces with moderate inclines.
URL:https://gardens.duke.edu/event/holiday-greenery-build-your-own-wreath-5/
LOCATION:Onsite at Duke Gardens – directions to follow
CATEGORIES:Adult Programs
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://gardens.duke.edu/wp-content/uploads/2024-Holiday-Card-Bodine_Historic-7779-002.jpg
END:VEVENT
