X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Calendar 1 Ics": "https://calendar.unc.edu/event/service-of-remembrance-for-james-seay"}
X-SOURCE-ID:calendar_1_ics
X-SOURCE:UNC Chapel Hill
DTSTAMP:20261114T061632Z
UID:tag:localist.com\,2008:EventInstance_54364363552510
DTSTART:20261206T190000Z
DTEND:20261206T210000Z
DESCRIPTION:A service of remembrance for the late poet and longtime UNC-Cha
 pel Hill writing professor James (Jim) Seay will be held on Sunday\, Decem
 ber 6th\, 2026\, at 2 p.m. at the Horace Williams House in Chapel Hill.  P
 rofessor Seay\, who taught at Carolina from 1974 till 2014\, died in Chape
 l Hill in July at the age of 87.\n\n \n\n \n\nA native Mississippian\, Sea
 y was a vigorous outdoorsman\, fisherman and hunter\, and wrote of his ven
 tures afield in his last book of essays\, Come! Come! Where? Where? (UNC P
 ress). He was well and widely known for his celebrated volumes of poetry\,
  including:  Let Not Your Heart (1970)\, Water Tables (1974)\, The Light a
 s They Found It (1990)\, and Open Field\, Understory (1997). In 1988 he re
 ceived the Award in Literature from the American Academy of Arts and Lette
 rs.\n\n \n\nThe December 6th service will be conducted by UNC’s Creative
  Writing Program (which Professor Seay directed 1987-1997) and the Departm
 ent of English and Comparative Literature.
GEO:35.9132;-79.055845
LOCATION:Horace Williams House
SUMMARY:Service of Remembrance for James Seay
URL;VALUE=URI:https://calendar.unc.edu/event/service-of-remembrance-for-jam
 es-seay
CATEGORIES:Ceremony
END:VEVENT
