DESCRIPTION:Calling all water-loving educators!!!\n\nJoin the NC Museum of 
 Natural Sciences this November to explore North Carolina’s beautiful Coh
 arie River. We will learn about the Riverkeepers restoration initiatives a
 nd hear directly from members of the Coharie Tribe about their experiences
  living along the river. Become familiar with one of North Carolina’s wi
 ld areas and connect with the long history of the people who call this lan
 d home. \n\nThis is an day-long event on Wednesday\, December 9th. Cost: $
 75 (this includes the kayak rental and lunch). Participants will ride with
  the group from Raleigh departing at 8:30am. Transportation will be in Mus
 eum vans or bus.\n\nRead more and register HERE! If registration is full\,
  be sure to join the waiting list.\n\nThe full workshop fee is due when yo
 u register and payment is via credit card. Registration for most Educator 
 Treks is on a first-come\, first-served basis. Treks fill quickly\, so reg
 ister early!
LOCATION:Depart from North Carolina Museum of Natural Sciences
SUMMARY:Sold Out: Educator Trek: Great Coharie River Paddling Tour
