X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Events 1 Ics": "https://events.dncr.nc.gov/event/community-stories-sustaining-north-carolinas-black-heritage"}
X-SOURCE-ID:events_1_ics
X-SOURCE:NC Cultural Resources
DTSTAMP:20261114T061600Z
UID:tag:localist.com\,2008:EventInstance_53138242023500
DTSTART:20261224T150000Z
DTEND:20261224T220000Z
DESCRIPTION:Community Stories: Sustaining North Carolina’s Black Heritage
  at the Gregg Museum of Art & Design presents a series of vignettes explor
 ing spaces of dignity\, belonging\, safety\, and imagination within Black 
 communities across North Carolina. Featuring historical photographs\, cont
 emporary images\, artworks from the Gregg Museum collection including a ha
 ndmade guitar by Freeman Vines\, and ephemera from community partners\, th
 e exhibition reflects on place\, memory\, creativity\, and spiritual resil
 ience across generations. Through stories of triumph and adversity\, Commu
 nity Stories honors the ways Black Americans have sustained and uplifted t
 heir communities through family\, entrepreneurship\, cultural expression\,
  and soulful imagination\, while inspiring future generations.
GEO:35.784925;-78.661662
LOCATION:Gregg Museum of Art & Design
SUMMARY:Community Stories: Sustaining North Carolina’s Black Heritage
URL;VALUE=URI:https://events.dncr.nc.gov/event/community-stories-sustaining
 -north-carolinas-black-heritage
CATEGORIES:Exhibits & Tours
CATEGORIES:Exhibitions
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-ID:gcal_b32e7018b18e1a8650f0d178e5d8314fd6664c368233eead570b44e368f882c9
SUMMARY:What’s the Plan? A Weekly Discussion with Indivisible’s Co-Fou
 nders
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20261224T150000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20261224T160000
DTSTAMP:20261114T061530Z
UID:3h0snhtuuutmutn5t53bin9jfl_R20260108T200000@google.com__20261224
SEQUENCE:2
CREATED:20250728T004006Z
DESCRIPTION:Link to join: <a href="https://www.mobilize.us/indivisible/ev
 ent/874938/?utm_medium=email&amp\;utm_source=substack">https://www.mobiliz
 e.us/indivisible/event/874938/?utm_medium=email&amp\;utm_source=substack</
 a><br><br>The onslaught of news\, the chaos coming out of the White House 
 – it’s all meant to overwhelm us. It’s a deliberate strategy to sow 
 confusion and make us believe we are powerless to fight back.<br><br>The a
 ntidote: Coming together in community to process what’s happening\, to s
 ift through what’s important and what’s just noise\, and coalesce arou
 nd strategies for fighting back.<br><br>Join Indivisible co-founders Leah 
 Greenberg and Ezra Levin each week\, as we carve out an hour to discuss wh
 at’s happening and – more importantly – what’s the plan.<br><br><a
  href="https://www.mobilize.us/indivisible/event/773746/" target="_blank">
 https://www.mobilize.us/indivisible/event/773746/</a>
LAST-MODIFIED:20260105T130328Z
