BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Resilientdurhamnc": "https://resilientdurhamnc.org/event/applications-open-tedxchavisway-youth/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:resilientdurhamnc
X-SOURCE:Resilient Durham NC
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270104
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270105
DTSTAMP:20261112T153529Z
CREATED:20261109T210324Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20261112T153529Z
UID:5209-1799020800-1799107199@resilientdurhamnc.org
SUMMARY:Applications Open: TEDxChavisWay Youth
DESCRIPTION:Applications are open for TEDxChavisWay Youth\, an independently organized TED event happening on May 1\, 2027 at the John Chavis Memorial Community Center in Raleigh. Youth between the ages of 10 and 19 who may be interested in speaking or performing at the event are encouraged to apply by the deadline\, January 4th. The full application link can be found here. \nTEDxChavisWay Youth is curated by a team of volunteers in partnership with NC State Extension program #PassTheMicYouth\, Wake County 4-H\, and Raleigh Parks and Recreation. Their goal is to bring together bright young minds to give talks that are idea-focused to foster learning\, inspiration and wonder—and provoke conversations that matter. \nTalks will be filmed and edited and videos will be hosted on the TEDx YouTube channel. All speakers will be assigned a coach to guide them through the process of crafting a talk\, from script to stage. Talks should be at or around 5 minutes on any topic related to the theme Speak Up\, Speak Out\, which celebrates young visionaries\, storytellers\, and changemakers who are shaping the world through the power of their voices and ideas. (Note: The theme is open to each individual’s interpretation). Performances can be up to 5 minutes and can include original music\, spoken word poetry\, dance\, and other forms of artistic expression.
URL:https://resilientdurhamnc.org/event/applications-open-tedxchavisway-youth/
LOCATION:John Chavis Memorial Community Center\, 505 Martin Luther King Jr Blvd\, Raleigh\, NC\, 27601\, United States
CATEGORIES:Youth Events
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Calendar Group African American Cultural Center": "https://calendar.ncsu.edu/event/you-are-here-geolocating-the-self-through-the-familiar-in-the-midst-of-the-unfamiliar-exhibition"}
X-SOURCE-ID:calendar_group_african_american_cultural_center
X-SOURCE:NC State African American Cultural Center
DTSTAMP:20261114T061046Z
UID:tag:localist.com\,2008:EventInstance_53550588361677
DTSTART:20270104T150000Z
DTEND:20270104T220000Z
DESCRIPTION:Join the African American Cultural Center to experience ariana 
 Farquharson's You Are Here: Geolocating the Self through the Familiar in t
 he Midst of the Unfamiliar. The exhibition is a speculative\, immersive wo
 rld-building study that invites guests to explore (geo)locating self and h
 ome amid a rapidly and frequently changing post-pandemic “new” world. 
 It will be on display in the art gallery at the African American Cultural 
 Center from Oct. 28\, 2026\, to  Feb. 28\, 2027. A behind-the-scenes look 
 at the exhibition is set for Nov. 11.
GEO:35.785108;-78.674529
LOCATION:Witherspoon Student Center\, African American Cultural Center (218
 )
SUMMARY:You Are Here Exhibition
URL;VALUE=URI:https://calendar.ncsu.edu/event/you-are-here-geolocating-the-
 self-through-the-familiar-in-the-midst-of-the-unfamiliar-exhibition
CATEGORIES:Community Events
CATEGORIES:Exhibitions
END:VEVENT
