SUMMARY:Survivor Roots Support Group
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20270128T173000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20270128T190000
DTSTAMP:20261114T061542Z
UID:0jeueh5ls2nkato3eog9u4dvh0_R20270128T223000@google.com__20270128
SEQUENCE:0
CREATED:20260628T195033Z
DESCRIPTION: This is a HYBRID support group that meets the 2nd &amp\; 4th
  Thursday\, folks can join in person or online. This group is available to
  anyone who is:<br><ul><li>LGBTQIA+</li><li>a survivor of abuse (intimate 
 partner violence\, family violence\, or any other kind of relational abuse
 )</li><li>North Carolina resident</li></ul><br>At the Southern Queer Survi
 vor Network\, we believe in the power of community-driven healing. A root 
 of survivorship is community\, something many Queer and Trans people find 
 themselves without after surviving interpersonal violence. We are committe
 d to creating a space where healing isn’t just about individual recovery
 —it’s about liberation from the systems that harm us.<br><br>~ Survivo
 r Roots ~ an ongoing support group intended to support our community\, pro
 vide consistency\, build &amp\; deepen connections among LGBTQ+ survivors 
 of interpersonal violence. This is a space where survivors can reclaim the
 ir narratives\, strengthen their resilience\, and build solidarity with on
 e another.<br><br>The aim of this support group is to:<br><ul><li>Foster c
 ommunity among survivors</li><li>Cultivate feelings of safety\, connection
 \, and validation</li><li>Provide education about signs and cycles of Quee
 r IPV</li><li>Promote healing\, and when necessary\, provide referral to m
 ental health professionals</li></ul><br>Register at the link in our bio or
  here: <a target="_blank" href="http://bit.ly/SurvivorRoots"><u>bit.ly/Sur
 vivorRoots</u></a><br>Location and meeting links will be disclosed AFTER s
 creening<br>Email <a target="_blank" href="mailto:advocate@lgbtqcenterofdu
 rham.org"><u>advocate@lgbtqcenterofdurham.org</u></a> with any questions!
LAST-MODIFIED:20261112T235436Z
LOCATION:Disclosed after screening
STATUS:CONFIRMED
TRANSP:OPAQUE
X-SOURCE:LGBTQ Center of Durham
END:VEVENT
