DESCRIPTION:For the past four years\, Living in Color has become a premiere
  Black History Month celebration of creativity\, shining a spotlight on ov
 er 100 artists of every medium\, style\, and stage in their artistic journ
 ey.\n\nCurated by Raleigh Film and Art Festival and hosted in partnership 
 with Dix Park\, this riveting exhibit is a month-long display of visual ar
 t representing the experience of people of color living in the south.
GEO:35.77048;-78.656794
LOCATION:Dix Park\, Gregory Poole All Faiths Chapel
SUMMARY:Living in Color Exhibit
URL;VALUE=URI:https://events.dncr.nc.gov/event/living-in-color-exhibit
CATEGORIES:Exhibits & Tours
CATEGORIES:Exhibitions
