BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Events 1 Ics": "https://events.dncr.nc.gov/event/project-restore-educator-trek-where-swans-fly-bears-walk-and-wolves-howl"}
X-SOURCE-ID:events_1_ics
X-SOURCE:NC Cultural Resources
DTSTAMP:20261114T061601Z
UID:tag:localist.com\,2008:EventInstance_54496456513901
DTSTART:20270206T190000Z
DTEND:20270206T200000Z
DESCRIPTION:Experience one of the greatest wildlife spectacles in North Car
 olina – thousands of tundra swans\, snow geese\, and other waterfowl ove
 r-wintering in an area rich in wildlife such as black bears\, bobcats and 
 red wolves. Learn winter bird identification\, tips on preserving tracks a
 nd signs\, and ideas for incorporating wild creatures into your teaching. 
 We hope to have the opportunity to meet with a red wolf biologist to learn
  about the restoration and monitoring work being done with this endangered
  species.\n\nWith support from the US Fish and Wildlife Service\, Project 
 RESTORE (Rescuing Endangered Species Through Outreach\, Restoration\, and 
 Education) will feature a suite of educational opportunities for teachers 
 and students to participate in restoration and monitoring of imperiled and
  endangered species in eastern North Carolina.\n\nCredit: 20 contact hours
  toward CEUs or Criteria II/III for North Carolina’s Environmental Educa
 tion Certification Program\n\nLodging: The workshop fee covers a two-night
  hotel stay near the wildlife refuge\, double occupancy.\n\nTransportation
 : Participants can ride with the group from Raleigh departing at 2pm or me
 et us in Columbia\, NC in the evening. Transportation will be in Museum va
 ns.\n\nRegistration: register now! \n\nIf the workshop is full when you go
  to register\, please sign up for the waiting list!\n\n*The cost of this T
 rek is reduced due to a grant through the US Fish and Wildlife Service. Du
 e to this reduction of costs\, Friends of the Museum discounts are unavail
 able.\n\nDetails:\n\nFee: $170* (includes two nights double-occupancy hote
 l style lodging\, transportation\, and workshop materials)Requirements: Fo
 r educators (includes teachers\, administrators\, pre-service or substitut
 e teachers\; non-formal educators\; any adult working on their EE certific
 ation)Program Instructor(s): Megan Davis\, Danielle Pender\, Rory McCollum
  and local expertsActivity Level: Hiking 2-3 miles on uneven surfaces.
GEO:35.782156;-78.639336
LOCATION:North Carolina Museum of Natural Sciences
SUMMARY:Project RESTORE Educator Trek: Where Swans Fly\, Bears Walk\, and W
 olves Howl
URL;VALUE=URI:https://events.dncr.nc.gov/event/project-restore-educator-tre
 k-where-swans-fly-bears-walk-and-wolves-howl
CATEGORIES:Education Programs
CATEGORIES:Workshops & Trainings
CATEGORIES:Outdoor & Recreation
CATEGORIES:Nature & Wildlife Programs
END:VEVENT
