BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Calendar 1 Ics": "https://calendar.unc.edu/event/ai-agents-in-survey-research-foundations-applications-oversight-and-evaluation"}
X-SOURCE-ID:calendar_1_ics
X-SOURCE:UNC Chapel Hill
DTSTAMP:20261114T061632Z
UID:tag:localist.com\,2008:EventInstance_54416751351487
DTSTART:20270223T150000Z
DTEND:20270223T210000Z
DESCRIPTION:This course explores the emerging role of AI agents in survey r
 esearch. Designed for survey practitioners\, data scientists\, and social 
 scientists\, it introduces agentic AI as the next iteration of artificial 
 intelligence technologies to be integrated with survey research methods. B
 uilding on foundational concepts in generative AI\, the course examines ho
 w agents differ from the previous iteration of LLMs and considers their po
 tential uses across the survey research lifecycle.\nParticipants will lear
 n core technical concepts around agentic AI\, approaches to evaluating age
 nt performance in the survey context\, the challenges of designing\, imple
 menting\, and assessing agentic workflows\, responsible AI deployment\, AI
 -assisted vs AI-driven paradigms of work\, and the role of human expertise
  in survey research. We will also examine bias in agentic systems\, the im
 plications of delegating research tasks to AI\, and strategies for maintai
 ning meaningful human oversight. Using data harmonization as a central app
 lication\, the course will draw on emerging empirical research and practic
 al examples to explore both the opportunities and limitations of agentic A
 I in survey research.\n\nRegistration and fee (refundable for UNCCH studen
 ts upon attendance) are required for Zoom link access.
LOCATION:
SUMMARY:AI Agents in Survey Research: Foundations\, Applications\, Oversigh
 t\, and Evaluation
URL;VALUE=URI:https://calendar.unc.edu/event/ai-agents-in-survey-research-f
 oundations-applications-oversight-and-evaluation
CATEGORIES:Workshops and Classes
END:VEVENT
