X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Calendar 1 Ics": "https://calendar.unc.edu/event/foundations-of-applied-mixed-methods-research-design"}
X-SOURCE-ID:calendar_1_ics
X-SOURCE:UNC Chapel Hill
DTSTAMP:20261114T061632Z
UID:tag:localist.com\,2008:EventInstance_54364870114852
DTSTART:20270319T140000Z
DTEND:20270319T200000Z
DESCRIPTION:This workshop provides participants with practical instruction 
 on the topics of integrating qualitative and quantitative data\, and the e
 ssential principles behind designing fundable mixed methods research. Spec
 ific topics include crafting mixed methods objectives and research questio
 ns\, choosing appropriate sampling strategies\, and selecting the most eff
 ective data collection methods (qualitative and quantitative). A significa
 nt amount of time is spent demonstrating the nuts and bolts of integrating
  qualitative and quantitative datasets\, including diagramming points of i
 nterface. Although this workshop is primarily embedded in an applied conte
 xt\, the instructors will present some of the more common typologies and n
 omenclature used in the field. Course structure includes lecture\, interac
 tive discussion\, and hands-on exercises.\n\nRegistration and fee (refunda
 ble for UNCCH students upon attendance) are required for Zoom access.
LOCATION:
SUMMARY:Foundations of Applied Mixed Methods Research Design
URL;VALUE=URI:https://calendar.unc.edu/event/foundations-of-applied-mixed-m
 ethods-research-design
CATEGORIES:Workshops and Classes
END:VEVENT
