X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Calendar 1 Ics": "https://calendar.unc.edu/event/integrated-mixed-methods-5305"}
X-SOURCE-ID:calendar_1_ics
X-SOURCE:UNC Chapel Hill
DTSTAMP:20261114T061632Z
UID:tag:localist.com\,2008:EventInstance_54488501805828
DTSTART:20270324T130000Z
DTEND:20270324T190000Z
DESCRIPTION:Mixed methods research (MMR) refers to research design and impl
 ementation that combines qualitative and quantitative data collection and/
 or analysis strategies. This seminar explores strategies for effectively d
 esigning\, implementing\, and integrating MMR. Through discussion of exemp
 lars and theoretical frameworks\, we will consider best practices for “m
 ixing” methods and presenting integrated findings. Participants will gai
 n practical skills for aligning methodological choices with research quest
 ions\, implementing complementary qualitative and quantitative techniques\
 , and articulating cohesive and rigorous mixed methods results.\n\n \n\nRe
 gistration and fee (refundable for UNC-Chapel Hill students upon attendanc
 e) are required for Zoom link access.
LOCATION:
SUMMARY:Integrated Mixed Methods
URL;VALUE=URI:https://calendar.unc.edu/event/integrated-mixed-methods-5305
CATEGORIES:Workshops and Classes
END:VEVENT
