DTEND:20270424T160000Z
DESCRIPTION:Prepare\, pin and mount a variety of spectacular tropical butte
 rflies. Learn the various techniques used to catch\, preserve and mount th
 ese and other fascinating arthropods. Explore the possibilities of insect 
 collecting in your backyard.\n\nCredit: 3 contact hours toward CEUs or Cri
 teria III for North Carolina’s Environmental Education Certification Pro
 gram\nUpon completion of the Trek\, you will receive a Certificate of Cour
 se Completion that includes the number of contact hours to turn in for CEU
 s. For those seeking Environmental Education Certification\, you will also
  receive an EE Form for up to 3 hours of credit.\n\nRegistration: register
  now!\nThe full workshop fee is due when you register and payment is via c
 redit card. Registration for most Educator Treks is on a first-come\, firs
 t-served basis. Treks fill quickly\, so register early!\n\nNote: We do not
  want cost to be a barrier for any educator. If the cost of this workshop 
 would prevent your participation\, please reach out to Megan Davis.\n\nDet
 ails:\n\nFee: $70* (includes insect resource manual\, pinning board\, butt
 erfly display box\, numerous exotic butterfly specimens)Requirements: For 
 educators (includes teachers\, administrators\, pre-service or substitute 
 teachers\; non-formal educators\; anyone working on their EE certification
 )Program Instructor(s): Andy Kauffman\, Colin BrammerActivity Level: Easy:
  Workshop will take place indoors in a lab settingCategories: Educator Tre
 ks\, Educators\, WorkshopsVenue\nNatural World Investigate Lab\nNature Res
 earch Center\nDowntown Raleigh- NRC\n121 West Jones Street\nRaleigh\, NC 2
 7601 United States
GEO:35.782156;-78.639336
LOCATION:North Carolina Museum of Natural Sciences\, Natural World Investig
 ate Lab
SUMMARY:Educator Trek: Butterfly Pinning and Backyard Bug Collecting
URL;VALUE=URI:https://events.dncr.nc.gov/event/educator-trek-butterfly-pinn
 ing-and-backyard-bug-collecting-6917
CATEGORIES:Education Programs
CATEGORIES:Workshops & Trainings
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Events 1 Ics": "https://events.dncr.nc.gov/event/hidden-battleship-tour-9482"}
X-SOURCE-ID:events_1_ics
X-SOURCE:NC Cultural Resources
DTSTAMP:20261114T061602Z
UID:tag:localist.com\,2008:EventInstance_53453763937062
DTSTART:20270424T150000Z
DTEND:20270424T210000Z
DESCRIPTION:Offered only four times this coming year\, Hidden Battleship ta
 kes adventurous visitors beyond the traditional self-guided tour and into 
 unrestored areas of the Battleship North Carolina Memorial that are normal
 ly closed to the public. Led by experienced guides in small groups\, parti
 cipants explore spaces deep below deck\, throughout the third deck\, in th
 e bow\, and high into the Ship's superstructure—including all the way to
  the top.\n\nThe 2027 Hidden Battleship tours will be offered on:\n\nSatur
 day\, February 27Saturday\, March 20Saturday\, April 24Saturday\, November
  20Each tour runs from 11:00 am to 5:00 pm. The cost is $75 per participan
 t\, plus tax.\n\nDesigned for adventurous history enthusiasts\, the six-ho
 ur experience requires climbing ladders\, crossing high hatches\, and navi
 gating tight and confined spaces. For that reason\, the program is limited
  to participants ages 16 and older.\n\n"Every compartment aboard the Battl
 eship has a story\," said Dr. Jay Martin\, Executive Director of Battleshi
 p North Carolina Memorial. "Hidden Battleship opens doors that are normall
 y closed\, inviting visitors to step into the spaces where sailors lived\,
  worked\, and fought—and to experience the Ship in a way very few people
  ever will."\n\nBecause attendance is intentionally limited to provide a s
 afe\, behind-the-scenes experience\, Hidden Battleship consistently sells 
 out well in advance. The experience has become a favorite among repeat vis
 itors\, military history enthusiasts\, photographers\, and anyone looking 
 to explore a side of the Ship that few ever have the opportunity to see.\n
 \nWhether you're searching for a memorable gift or your next great adventu
 re\, Hidden Battleship offers an unforgettable behind-the-scenes experienc
 e unlike any other.\n\nVisitors are encouraged to reserve their spots earl
 y. Tickets and additional information are available at https://bit.ly/hidd
 enbattleship
GEO:34.236158;-77.953643
LOCATION: Battleship North Carolina
SUMMARY:Hidden Battleship Tour
URL;VALUE=URI:https://events.dncr.nc.gov/event/hidden-battleship-tour-9482
CATEGORIES:Education Programs
CATEGORIES:Exhibits & Tours
CATEGORIES:Guided Tours
CATEGORIES:Special Site Programs
END:VEVENT
